SND01 "sine" -- UI sounds

UI sounds: SND01 "sine" by Yasuhiro Tsuchiya, from SND (snd.dev) by Dentsu Inc. CX Creative Center.

Source: https://snd.dev/ (SND01_sine.zip)
Licence: snd.dev Terms of Use (free use including commercial; credit appreciated; no redistribution of the unprocessed materials by themselves; no use as a trademark sound logo). The snd-lib project that distributes these sounds publishes its source code under the MIT licence.

Terms of Use (summary of the snd.dev Terms of Use as recorded when Bloom adopted the pack):
  - Free use, commercial use included. Credit is appreciated.
  - Redistributing the unprocessed materials by themselves is prohibited.
  - Using the materials as a trademark sound logo is prohibited.

Bloom does not redistribute the pack. It bundles a small set of derived sounds that were trimmed
of silence, resampled to 48 kHz, level-matched, peak-limited and converted to 16-bit mono WAV.
The unmodified archive is not part of this repository or of any Bloom build. The exact selection,
processing steps and file digests are recorded in src/ui/sound/assets/provenance.md.

The sounds play only for Bloom's own interface feedback (render and import results, warnings and,
when the artist turns them on, interaction cues). They are not used as a trademark or sound logo.
